1
00:00:03,320 --> 00:00:06,880
John Snow Defeats King Cholera

2
00:00:09,040 --> 00:00:15,700
John Snow was a famous doctor in London, so expert indeed that he attended Queen Victoria

3
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:24,680
But he became inspired when he thought about helping ordinary people exposed to cholera.

4
00:00:25,920 --> 00:00:28,960
This was the deadly disease of its day.

5
00:00:29,260 --> 00:00:32,400
Neither its cause nor its cure was understood.

6
00:00:33,580 --> 00:00:38,440
So many thousands of terrified people died every time there was an outbreak.

7
00:00:39,620 --> 00:00:43,160
John Snow wanted to face the challenge and solve this problem.

8
00:00:44,260 --> 00:00:49,020
He knew that cholera would never be controlled until its cause was found.

9
00:00:50,380 --> 00:00:56,100
He became interested in two theories that possibly explained how cholera killed people.

10
00:00:57,500 --> 00:01:01,380
The first suggested that cholera multiplied in the air.

11
00:01:01,960 --> 00:01:06,460
A cloud of dangerous gas floated around until it found its victims.

12
00:01:14,100 --> 00:01:20,320
From the stomach the disease quickly attacked the body and soon the affected person died.

13
00:01:22,060 --> 00:01:27,080
John Snow suspected that the second theory was correct but he needed evidence.

14
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:46,100
In two particular streets, the cholera outbreak was so severe

15
00:01:46,100 --> 00:01:50,140
that more than 500 people died in ten days.

16
00:01:50,760 --> 00:01:53,300
He was determined to find out why.

17
00:01:54,660 --> 00:01:59,900
First he marked on a map the exact places where all the dead people had lived.

18
00:02:00,640 --> 00:02:04,140
This gave him a valuable clue about the cause of the disease.

19
00:02:05,280 --> 00:02:10,780
Many of the deaths were near the water pump in Broad Street (especially numbers 16,

20
00:02:11,240 --> 00:02:13,960
37, 38 and 40).

21
00:02:15,240 --> 00:02:20,560
He also noticed that some houses (such as 20 and 21 Broad Street

22
00:02:20,560 --> 00:02:24,660
and 8 and 9 Cambridge Street) had had no deaths.

23
00:02:25,540 --> 00:02:29,680
He had not foreseen this, so he made further investigations.

24
00:02:31,100 --> 00:02:35,560
He discovered that these people worked in the pub at 7 Cambridge Street.

25
00:02:36,340 --> 00:02:40,460
They had been given free beer and so had not drunk the water from the pump.

26
00:02:41,160 --> 00:02:43,800
It seemed that the water was to blame.

27
00:02:51,340 --> 00:02:55,780
He found that it came from the river polluted by the dirty water from London.

28
00:02:57,140 --> 00:03:02,360
He immediately told the astonished people in Broad Street to remove the handle from the pump

29
00:03:02,360 --> 00:03:04,580
so that it could not be used.

30
00:03:05,320 --> 00:03:08,280
Soon afterwards the disease slowed down.

31
00:03:08,860 --> 00:03:14,240
He had shown that cholera was spread by germs and not in a cloud of gas.

32
00:03:15,800 --> 00:03:20,060
In another part of London, he found supporting evidence from two other deaths

33
00:03:20,060 --> 00:03:22,220
that were linked to the Broad Street outbreak.

34
00:03:23,120 --> 00:03:25,380
A woman, who had moved away from Broad Street,

35
00:03:25,380 --> 00:03:31,660
liked the water from the pump so much that she had it delivered to her house every day.

36
00:03:31,800 --> 00:03:36,160
Both she and her daughter died of cholera after drinking the water.

37
00:03:37,080 --> 00:03:41,560
With this extra evidence John Snow was able to announce with certainty

38
00:03:41,560 --> 00:03:44,560
that polluted water carried the virus.

39
00:03:46,260 --> 00:03:48,240
To prevent this from happening again,

40
00:03:48,520 --> 00:03:52,880
John Snow suggested that the source of all the water supplies be examined.

41
00:03:59,420 --> 00:04:03,060
Finally "King Cholera" was defeated.
